  the ukrainians have uh counter-attacked  in certain areas but ultimately the  ukrainians have got about four and a  half thousand troops we don't know how  many of them are still on their feet but  they had about fourteen four and a half  thousand the russians surround them with  that three times that number fourteen  thousand and the russians can bring up  more troops the nearest troops who could  help the ukrainians in mario paul are  probably about 60 miles away so given  that president putin has made it clear  he wants to take mario paul probably  before the 9th of may which is his great  victory parade and speeches then i think  the uh the next couple of weeks we'll  decide mario paul one way or the other  if we were to zoom out again and just uh  consider all of uh ukraine clearly a lot  of discussion about a renewed offensive  more broadly on the donbass region not  just mario pole  how much does the extra troops that  russia's moving there changed the  bargain there because of course they  were slow to make progress there as well  over the last couple they are i i mean  the fact is it's easier a country for  armoured vehicles and tanks but they've  left it until the spring which was very  soft the time to use armored vehicles in  ukraine is in the winter when it's cold  when frozen or in the summer when it's  hot and dusty and dry but the autumn of  the spring is exactly the wrong time to  try an armored uh thrust which the  russians must have thought they would  not have to do  and the ukrainians are very well dug in  in the donbass region they've been there  for since 2014 they've been there for  eight years so i think it may be a  monumental battle developing and  everybody knows that the the war will  depend on what now happens in the  donbass that this will either give  russia as it were a way out uh which  shows that they've grabbed a bit more  territory or it will push them back  again and it will create a stalemate and  leave putin in an even bigge